{"alignments": [{"id": "PSA.114.1.a001", "note": "Temporal בְּ + infinitive construct recast as a finite temporal clause; the preposition takes the *when* (rule 52).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.1.001"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.1.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "PSA.114.1.a002", "note": "Infinitive construct keeps the verb; *forth* is the phrasal particle completing the going-out lexeme (rule 44), head on *went*.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.1.002"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.1.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t003", "t004"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "PSA.114.1.a003", "note": "Subject of the infinitive, reordered before the verb in English.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.1.003"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.1.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002"], "target_head": "t002"}, {"id": "PSA.114.1.a004", "note": "מִן → *out of*, headed on *out* which carries the ablative lexeme (rule 24).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.1.004"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.1.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005", "t006"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "PSA.114.1.a005", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.1.005"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.1.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "PSA.114.1.a006", "note": "Construct noun with no article morpheme takes the supplied *The* (rule 29).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.1.006"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.1.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008", "t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "PSA.114.1.a007", "note": "Nomen rectum takes the *of* (rule 19).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.1.007"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.1.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010", "t011"], "target_head": "t011"}, {"id": "PSA.114.1.a008", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.1.008"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.1.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t012"], "target_head": "t012"}, {"id": "PSA.114.1.a009", "note": "Indefinite article belongs to the noun (rule 15).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.1.009"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.1.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t013", "t014"], "target_head": "t014"}, {"id": "PSA.114.1.a010", "note": "Attributive participle לָעַז 'speaking a foreign tongue' recast as *of strange language*; the *of* and both words are the ASV's rendering of this one participle (rule 31), no second source nominal stands for rule 19. Headed on *strange*, which carries the foreignness; *language* is a defensible alternative head.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.1.010"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.1.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t015", "t016", "t017"], "target_head": "t016"}], "ref": "PSA.114.1", "review_notes": ["Whole-verse temporal clause; no verb in the second colon, none supplied by the ASV."], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
{"alignments": [{"id": "PSA.114.2.a001", "note": "Resultative הָיָה לְ: the verb takes *became* and the לְ is left with nothing (rule 21).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.2.001"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.2.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002"], "target_head": "t002"}, {"id": "PSA.114.2.a002", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.2.002"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.2.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "PSA.114.2.a003", "note": "Resultative לְ silenced by the *became* recasting on הָיָה (rule 21).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.2.003"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.2.003", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "PSA.114.2.a004", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.2.004"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.2.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "PSA.114.2.a005", "note": "Possessive suffix (rule 18).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.2.005"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.2.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t003"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "PSA.114.2.a006", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.2.006"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.2.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "PSA.114.2.a007", "note": "Gapped colon; the ASV supplies no copula, so nothing further to place (rule 34). Hebrew plural rendered singular.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.2.007"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.2.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "PSA.114.2.a008", "note": "Possessive suffix (rule 18).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.2.008"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.2.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t006"], "target_head": "t006"}], "ref": "PSA.114.2", "review_notes": [], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
{"alignments": [{"id": "PSA.114.3.a001", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.3.001"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.3.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "PSA.114.3.a002", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.3.002"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.3.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002"], "target_head": "t002"}, {"id": "PSA.114.3.a003", "note": "Verb keeps only *saw*; the supplied object is placed separately (rule 44).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.3.003"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.3.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t003"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "PSA.114.3.a004", "note": "Supplied object pronoun with no object morpheme in the Hebrew (rule 44).", "source": [], "source_head": null, "status": "added", "target": ["t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "PSA.114.3.a005", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.3.004"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.3.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "PSA.114.3.a006", "note": "Waw-consecutive verb takes the verb; the waw takes *and* (rule 14).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.3.005"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.3.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "PSA.114.3.a007", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.3.006"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.3.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "PSA.114.3.a008", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.3.007"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.3.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "PSA.114.3.a009", "note": "סָבַב 'turned' rendered by the passive *was driven*; auxiliary stays with the verb, head on the lexical verb (rule 17).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.3.008"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.3.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009", "t010"], "target_head": "t010"}, {"id": "PSA.114.3.a010", "note": "לְאָחוֹר recast as the single adverb *back*; preposition and noun share the unit headed on the noun (rule 40, as בְּאָחוֹר → *back*).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.3.009", "WLC.PSA.114.3.010"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.3.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t011"], "target_head": "t011"}], "ref": "PSA.114.3", "review_notes": [], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
{"alignments": [{"id": "PSA.114.4.a001", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.4.001"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.4.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "PSA.114.4.a002", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.4.002"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.4.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002"], "target_head": "t002"}, {"id": "PSA.114.4.a003", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.4.003"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.4.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t003"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "PSA.114.4.a004", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.4.004"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.4.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "PSA.114.4.a005", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.4.005"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.4.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "PSA.114.4.a006", "note": "גִּבְעָה rendered *The little hills*: supplied *The* is the noun's (rule 15) and *little* is the ASV's specifier distinguishing hills from mountains; the ASV writes bare *hills* for this word elsewhere, so the head stays on *hills* (rule 31). *little* is not `added`.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.4.006"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.4.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t006", "t007", "t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "PSA.114.4.a007", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.4.007"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.4.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "PSA.114.4.a008", "note": "Construct chain 'young of sheep' fused into the one word *lambs*, which writes both lexemes; head on the construct standing first (rules 30, 23). s009 is the competing head.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.4.008", "WLC.PSA.114.4.009"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.4.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010"], "target_head": "t010"}], "ref": "PSA.114.4", "review_notes": ["Gapped verb in the second colon; the ASV supplies none."], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
{"alignments": [{"id": "PSA.114.5.a001", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.5.001"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.5.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "PSA.114.5.a002", "note": "מַה־לְּךָ 'what is to thee': the predicate לְ takes *aileth*, the relational verb the ASV writes where the copula would stand (rules 49, 20). Competing reading: מַה + לְ as one noncompositional *What aileth*.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.5.002"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.5.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002"], "target_head": "t002"}, {"id": "PSA.114.5.a003", "note": "Suffix takes the pronoun written for it (rules 18, 40).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.5.003"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.5.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t003"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "PSA.114.5.a004", "note": "Vocative article; the ASV writes nothing for it (rule 36).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.5.004"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.5.004", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "PSA.114.5.a005", "note": "Vocative takes the supplied *O thou* (rule 36).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.5.005"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.5.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t004", "t005", "t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "PSA.114.5.a006", "note": "כִּי takes *that*; the ASV rewrites it over the juxtaposed second question, whose Hebrew writes no conjunction, so both occurrences are the one כִּי's discontinuous unit (rules 25, 55). Competing reading: second *that* `added` under rule 55.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.5.006"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.5.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007", "t012"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "PSA.114.5.a007", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.5.007"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.5.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008", "t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "PSA.114.5.a008", "note": "Vocative article; nothing written for it (rule 36).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.5.008"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.5.008", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "PSA.114.5.a009", "note": "Vocative takes the supplied *Thou* (rule 36).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.5.009"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.5.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010", "t011"], "target_head": "t011"}, {"id": "PSA.114.5.a010", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.5.010"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.5.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t013", "t014"], "target_head": "t014"}, {"id": "PSA.114.5.a011", "note": "לְאָחוֹר → *back*, one unit headed on the noun (rule 40).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.5.011", "WLC.PSA.114.5.012"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.5.012", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t015"], "target_head": "t015"}], "ref": "PSA.114.5", "review_notes": [], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
