{"alignments": [{"id": "PSA.114.7.a001", "note": "Compound preposition מִלִּ rendered by the single *at*; heads on the first preposition (rule 23). Alternative: לְ `unrepresented` beside מִן → *at*.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.7.001", "WLC.PSA.114.7.002"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.7.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "PSA.114.7.a002", "note": "Here the ASV writes a word for פָּנֶה itself, so no fusion with the preposition (rule 30); supplied *the* on the construct (rule 29).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.7.003"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.7.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005", "t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "PSA.114.7.a003", "note": "Rectum takes the *of* (rule 19) and the supplied *the* (rule 15).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.7.004"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.7.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007", "t008", "t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "PSA.114.7.a004", "note": "Imperative keeps only *Tremble*; the *thou* is read as the vocative's, standing before the noun (rule 36).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.7.005"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.7.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "PSA.114.7.a005", "note": "Vocative takes *thou* (rule 36). The pronoun stands both after the imperative and before the noun; the ASV's comma sets it with *earth*. Competing reading: *thou* as the imperative's subject pronoun under rule 17.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.7.006"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.7.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002", "t003"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "PSA.114.7.a006", "note": "Compound preposition → *At*, headed on the first (rule 23).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.7.007", "WLC.PSA.114.7.008"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.7.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010"], "target_head": "t010"}, {"id": "PSA.114.7.a007", "note": "פָּנֶה rendered *the presence* with a supplied *the* (rule 29).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.7.009"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.7.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t011", "t012"], "target_head": "t012"}, {"id": "PSA.114.7.a008", "note": "Rectum of the outer chain takes *of*; construct of the inner chain takes the supplied *the* (rules 19, 29).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.7.010"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.7.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t013", "t014", "t015"], "target_head": "t015"}, {"id": "PSA.114.7.a009", "note": "Rectum takes *of* (rule 19).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.7.011"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.7.011", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t016", "t017"], "target_head": "t017"}], "ref": "PSA.114.7", "review_notes": ["ASV reorders the vocative clause before the first prepositional phrase."], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
{"alignments": [{"id": "PSA.114.8.a001", "note": "Substantival article on the participle takes the supplied relative *Who* (rule 41).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.8.001"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.8.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "PSA.114.8.a002", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.8.002"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.8.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002"], "target_head": "t002"}, {"id": "PSA.114.8.a003", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.8.003"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.8.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t003"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "PSA.114.8.a004", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.8.004"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.8.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "PSA.114.8.a005", "note": "Bare second accusative of result with no preposition in the Hebrew; the supplied *into* states what the nominal contributes and belongs to it (rule 33), *a* the noun's (rule 15). The verb's own object is הַצּוּר, so rule 44 does not reach the word.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.8.005"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.8.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005", "t006", "t007"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "PSA.114.8.a006", "note": "Rectum takes *of* (rule 19).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.8.006"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.8.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008", "t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "PSA.114.8.a007", "note": "Supplied *The* belongs to the noun (rule 15).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.8.007"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.8.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010", "t011"], "target_head": "t011"}, {"id": "PSA.114.8.a008", "note": "Written לְ takes the *into* (rule 11).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.8.008"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.8.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t012"], "target_head": "t012"}, {"id": "PSA.114.8.a009", "note": "Indefinite article the noun's (rule 15).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.8.009"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.8.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t013", "t014"], "target_head": "t014"}, {"id": "PSA.114.8.a010", "note": "The projection segments a 3ms suffix on מַעְיְנוֹ; the ASV writes no pronoun for it (rule 40). Likely the archaic connecting vowel, but no textual decision is taken here (rule 9).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.8.010"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.8.010", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "PSA.114.8.a011", "note": "Rectum takes *of* (rule 19).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.114.8.011"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.114.8.011", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t015", "t016"], "target_head": "t016"}], "ref": "PSA.114.8", "review_notes": ["Second colon is gapped; the ASV supplies no verb."], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
